<header><a class="brand" href="#">CARVE BROS<span>WOOD. WITH MEANING.</span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#how">How it works</a><a href="#occasions">Gift ideas</a><a href="#faq">Questions</a></nav><a class="button small" href="#create">Create your keepsake</a></header>
<main><section class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="line"></span>SOUNDWOOD BY CARVE BROS</p><h1>Some voices<br>are worth<br><em>keeping.</em></h1><p class="intro">Their laugh. Your vows. A little “I love you.”<br>Turn a meaningful recording into a carved wood keepsake you can see, touch, and hear.</p><a class="button" href="#create">Make something personal</a><a class="text-link" href="#how">Discover how it works</a><div class="hero-meta">CUSTOM SOUNDWAVE ART <span>·</span> TAP TO LISTEN</div></div><div class="hero-image"><img src="{{ 'soundwood.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Soundwood concept: a walnut plaque with a carved soundwave and the words Love you, Mom" width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high"><span class="image-caption">A memory, made tangible. <small>Product concept shown</small></span></div></section>
<div class="statement"><span>YOUR ACTUAL RECORDING</span><span>PERSONALIZED WOOD ART</span><span>HIDDEN TAP-TO-LISTEN TAG</span><span>MADE BY CARVE BROS</span></div>
<section class="section story"><p class="eyebrow">MORE THAN A MESSAGE</p><h2>A beautiful piece of wood.<br><em>An unmistakably personal gift.</em></h2><div class="story-bottom"><p>Photos capture how a moment looked. Soundwood brings back how it sounded. We turn the shape of your recording into a carved waveform, then connect the piece to that same audio with a hidden NFC tag.</p><p>On the shelf, it’s a quiet reminder of someone you love. With a phone nearby, it becomes their voice again.</p></div></section>
<section class="section product-gallery"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">MADE TO BE HELD. MADE TO BE HEARD.</p><h2>Beautiful on display.<br><em>Personal when you tap.</em></h2></div><p>Every waveform tells a different story. The finished piece becomes part of the room until someone brings the memory back to life.</p></div><div class="gallery-grid"><figure class="gallery-primary"><img src="{{ 'soundwood-tap.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="A phone held beside the NFC mark on a walnut Soundwood plaque, showing the recording player" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>01</span><b>Tap to listen</b><small>Hold a compatible phone near the marked spot, open the prompt, and press play.</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="{{ 'soundwood-gift.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="A walnut Soundwood plaque displayed beside a kraft gift box and cream ribbon" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy"><figcaption><span>02</span><b>Ready for their moment</b><small>A one-of-one keepsake for the occasions that deserve more than another ordinary gift.</small></figcaption></figure></div><p class="fine gallery-note">Concept photography shown. Natural wood grain and finished details will vary by piece.</p></section><section id="how" class="section how"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM A VOICE TO A KEEPSAKE</p><h2>Small steps.<br><em>A lasting connection.</em></h2></div><p>No special equipment to record.<br>No dedicated app needed to listen on a compatible phone.</p></div><div class="steps"><article><span class="number">01</span><h3>Send a little something.</h3><p>Record a new message on your phone, or use an existing voice memo or audio clip. A clear voice and a quiet room work best.</p></article><article><span class="number">02</span><h3>Make it your own.</h3><p>Choose the words, names, or date you’d like engraved. We discuss the wood, layout, and size and confirm your design before carving.</p></article><article><span class="number">03</span><h3>Give them their moment.</h3><p>The carved waveform represents your recording. A hidden tag links to its listening page, ready to open with a compatible phone.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="listen section"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE LITTLE DETAIL THAT CHANGES EVERYTHING</p><h2>Tap the wood.<br><em>Hear the memory.</em></h2><p>A small NFC tag is tucked behind the marked listening spot. It holds a web link to your recording’s listening page. The tag itself needs no battery, charging, or Bluetooth pairing.</p><ol class="tap-steps"><li><b>Wake and unlock your phone.</b><span>On Android, make sure NFC is enabled.</span></li><li><b>Hold your phone close to the tap mark.</b><span>Use the top of an iPhone or the NFC area on an Android phone.</span></li><li><b>Open the link, then press play.</b><span>Tap the notification or browser prompt to hear the recording.</span></li></ol><p class="fine">An internet connection is required to open the listening page. The wood has no built-in speaker; audio plays through your phone or connected headphones.</p></div><aside class="listening-card"><span class="eyebrow">A SOUNDWOOD LISTENING PAGE</span><h3>“Love you, Mom.”</h3><p>A small voice. A big feeling.</p><div class="audio-art" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div><div class="play-label"><span>▶</span> YOUR ORIGINAL RECORDING</div><p class="fine">Illustrative listening-page preview</p><div class="compatibility"><b>iPhone & Android</b><p>iPhone XS / XR and newer support background URL-tag reading. Android support depends on the device and NFC settings.</p></div></aside></section>
<section id="occasions" class="section occasions"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">FOR THE PEOPLE WHO MATTER</p><h2>There’s a voice<br><em>for every occasion.</em></h2></div><p>The best recording isn’t always polished.<br>Sometimes it’s simply, completely them.</p></div><div class="occasion-grid">
<article><span>01 / FOR MOM</span><h3>Mother’s Day</h3><p>A chorus of “We love you, Mom,” a child’s laugh, or a thank-you for everything she does.</p><blockquote>“You make our world feel like home.”</blockquote></article>
<article><span>02 / FOR DAD</span><h3>Father’s Day</h3><p>His favorite little voices, a shared inside joke, or the words you don’t say often enough.</p><blockquote>“Thanks for always being there, Dad.”</blockquote></article>
<article><span>03 / ANOTHER YEAR</span><h3>Birthdays</h3><p>A birthday wish from the kids, a message from far away, or friends sharing favorite memories.</p><blockquote>“Here’s to more adventures with you.”</blockquote></article>
<article><span>04 / YOUR LOVE STORY</span><h3>Weddings & anniversaries</h3><p>Your vows, the proposal, or a message celebrating a life you’re building together.</p><blockquote>“I’d choose you all over again.”</blockquote></article>
<article><span>05 / THE LITTLE YEARS</span><h3>New babies & childhood</h3><p>First words, a bedtime “goodnight,” or a tiny laugh you wish you could bottle.</p><blockquote>“Love you to the moon and back.”</blockquote></article>
<article><span>06 / ALWAYS WITH YOU</span><h3>Remembrance</h3><p>A saved voicemail, a familiar greeting, or a loved one’s story, preserved with care.</p><blockquote>“It’s me. Just calling to say I love you.”</blockquote></article>
<article><span>07 / HOME FOR THE HOLIDAYS</span><h3>Christmas & grandparents</h3><p>A family greeting, grandchildren saying their names, or a holiday tradition in their own voices.</p><blockquote>“Merry Christmas, Grandma and Grandpa.”</blockquote></article>
<article><span>08 / A NEW CHAPTER</span><h3>Graduations & milestones</h3><p>Words of encouragement for a graduate, a retirement thank-you, or a message for someone moving away.</p><blockquote>“We’re so proud of who you’re becoming.”</blockquote></article>
<article><span>09 / JUST BECAUSE</span><h3>Everyday love</h3><p>An “I miss you,” a pet’s familiar sound, or an ordinary moment that means everything.</p><blockquote>“No occasion. Just you.”</blockquote></article></div><p class="fine examples">Messages above are inspiration for your recording.</p></section>
<section class="personalize section"><p class="eyebrow">ONE RECORDING. ENTIRELY YOURS.</p><h2>The sound is personal.<br><em>The details should be, too.</em></h2><div class="details-grid"><article><h3>Your waveform</h3><p>Created from your audio, so every piece has its own shape. Clear, high-contrast carving makes the sound part of the design.</p></article><article><h3>Your words</h3><p>Add a name, a meaningful date, or a short line that gives the recording context. Keep it simple or make it deeply personal.</p></article><article><h3>Your wood & format</h3><p>Discuss the wood tone, size, and display style with us. Natural grain varies, making each finished piece unique.</p></article><article><h3>Your listening experience</h3><p>The hidden tag points to a web page containing your recording. Ask about a backup written link or QR code for phones without NFC.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="create" class="section create"><div><p class="eyebrow">LET’S MAKE YOUR SOUNDWOOD</p><h2>Start with a voice.<br><em>We’ll help with the rest.</em></h2><p>Tell us who it’s for, what you’d like to capture, and when you need it. We’ll discuss the design and confirm pricing, availability, shipping, and recording-page details before you order.</p><p class="fine">Have an old recording? Keep the original file safe. Share only audio you own or have permission to use.</p></div><form id="inquiry"><label for="occasion">Who or what is it for?</label><select id="occasion"><option>Mother’s Day</option><option>Father’s Day</option><option>Birthday</option><option>Wedding / anniversary</option><option>Baby / childhood memory</option><option>Remembrance</option><option>Christmas / grandparents</option><option>Graduation / milestone</option><option>Just because</option></select><label for="message">Tell us about your idea</label><textarea id="message" rows="4" placeholder="A voice memo from our kids for their grandma, with their names engraved…"></textarea><label for="needed">When do you need it? <span>(optional)</span></label><input id="needed" type="date"><button class="button" type="submit">Prepare my inquiry</button><p class="fine">This prepares a message for you to share with Carve Bros. No payment or recording upload is required here.</p></form></section>
<section id="faq" class="section faq"><div><p class="eyebrow">A FEW GOOD QUESTIONS</p><h2>Before you<br><em>make a memory.</em></h2></div><div class="faq-items">
<details><summary>Does the person receiving it need an app?</summary><p>No dedicated Soundwood app is needed on a compatible phone. iPhone XS / XR and newer can read a web-link NFC tag in the background. Android phones must have NFC hardware and NFC enabled; exact prompts vary. Older phones may require an NFC reader app or a backup web link.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is the recording stored inside the wood?</summary><p>The tag stores the listening-page link, not the audio itself. Your recording is hosted online. The phone opens that page and plays the sound. The carved waveform is visual artwork; scanning the carved shape does not play audio.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I use an existing voicemail or video?</summary><p>An existing recording can make a meaningful keepsake. Save the original audio or video file rather than relying on a voicemail inbox. Tell us what you have so we can confirm whether the audio can be prepared for your piece.</p></details>
<details><summary>How long should my recording be?</summary><p>A short, clear message is a good starting point. A few heartfelt words can be enough. Ask about longer recordings or combining several voices before ordering; the layout and listening experience depend on your file.</p></details>
<details><summary>How private is the listening page?</summary><p>An unlisted link is not the same as a password-protected page. Anyone who has the link may be able to open or share it. Discuss access options before providing sensitive audio, especially recordings of children.</p></details>
<details><summary>Will it keep playing forever?</summary><p>Playback depends on the listening page and audio hosting remaining available. Confirm the hosting duration, any ongoing fees, and what happens if the service changes before ordering. Keep your original recording and ask for a downloadable backup.</p></details>
<details><summary>What are the price, delivery time, and return policy?</summary><p>These are confirmed with your custom quote. Your design, wood, size, and required date affect availability. Confirm the total price, shipping, proof approval, personalization changes, and return or damage policy before payment. For a holiday gift, contact us early.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I care for it, and what if tapping doesn’t work?</summary><p>Keep wood indoors and dry; dust gently with a soft cloth. To listen, unlock your phone, enable NFC where needed, and try different positions close to the marked spot. Metal or thick cases can interfere. Use your backup link if available.</p></details>
</div></section><section class="closing"><p class="eyebrow">THE MOMENT PASSES. THE VOICE MATTERS.</p><h2>Give them something<br><em>only you could give.</em></h2><a class="button" href="#create">Start your Soundwood</a></section></main>
